      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It sounds like you're drawing insightful parallels between historical logistical challenges and modern geopolitical tensions. Modern powers may be miscalculating the ripple effects by underestimating the resilience of global supply chains when faced with prolonged disruption. Specifically, they might be overlooking the cascading effects on secondary markets and smaller trading nation economies that rely heavily on timely transit through vital choke points. This historical weight of strategic error remains relevant, suggesting that overconfidence in securing passage is a common pitfall.",
